This leads to the browser blocking the subsequent actual request (e.g., POST /api/auth/phone-number/send-otp) with a CORS error, despite trustedOrigins being correctly configured on the server.

Specific Observations:


1. Server-to-Server Calls Work: When using Next.js Server Actions (which initiate requests server-to-server), authentication calls to ams.example.com succeed. However, any Set-Cookie headers are not automatically forwarded to the client's browser without manual intervention, which is a separate but related concern for cross-domain cookie handling. This confirms the underlying authentication logic on ams.example.com is functional.

